meta {
  name: Create Page-Level Org Mapping (no form_id)
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/page-org-map?tenant_id={{tenantId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "org_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "page_id": "123456789",
    "platform": "fb"
  }
}

docs {
  The page-level catch-all: no form_id, so EVERY leadgen form on this page
  routes to org_id unless a more specific form_id row exists for that same
  page. Kept as its own request because it is the case the API could not
  express at all until now, and the one the admin screen will create most.

  Expect 201 with form_id NULL on the created row. A second ACTIVE page-level
  row for the same page is refused with 409
  (uq_meta_page_form_org_map_page_level) — deactivate or edit the existing one
  instead.
}
